From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 06:00:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 019/105] glue: cached router zero-bias, fused FP8 KV
 scale+cast+store, router GEMV and MTP-entry kernels (flag-gated)

- topk.fused_topk: reuse one zero correction-bias tensor per (N, device)
  instead of torch.zeros per MoE layer (always on, semantically identical).
- SGLANG_KV_FP8_FUSED_STORE=1: one Triton kernel replaces div_/div_/to/to +
  store_cache for bf16->fp8_e4m3 NHD KV writes at N<=64 (bit-exact vs the
  reference path; 0-d tensor scales are rounded to bf16 first like torch
  promotion does).
- SGLANG_ROUTER_GEMV=1 (router_gemv.py) and SGLANG_MTP_ENTRY_FUSED=1
  (mtp_entry.py): numerically validated but SLOWER than the cuBLAS/reference
  paths on RTX PRO 6000 (7.5 vs 5.0us; 94-157 vs 63-75us) -> keep OFF.
- GPU tests: test/srt/layers/test_glue_d.py (13 passed).

Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.6-sol) from GLUE_D_SPEC.md; KV-store rounding fix,
test tolerance and review by the supervisor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
